# fpga/CURRENT: the ONE resolver for the currently qualified FPGA packages.
#
# Consumers (template protocol T-fpga.4/5, T-snn.10, paper snapshot tooling)
# read this file instead of spelling a package path in prose: a version stored
# in prose drifts the next time the datapath is re-qualified, while this file
# travels with the repo state it describes. Update it in the same commit that
# qualifies a new package (tests/test_fpga_current.py checks every path).
#
# One block per problem class. polyhedral = rows plus box bounds, no cones;
# conic = rows and bounds plus native Euclidean-ball and scaled-SOC resets.
# On the board, v07 with cones off matches the v06 native emulation records on
# the v06 parity bundle (one-shot), 6x18 (one-shot, persistent), and 20x60 and
# 64x64 (one-shot). v08 (2026-10-11) returns v06's raw state and telemetry
# byte for byte on the board (framework fixtures in both launch modes, forced
# STREAM/CG, and the economic-dispatch band fleet) and supersedes v06, which
# stays in the tree. Which polyhedral image a problem uses is the routing
# rule below.
#
# Routing within the polyhedral class (measured 2026-10-24; the ED fleet
# comparison is in fpga/kv260_v09_bram/evidence/ed_fleet_2026-10-24/, the
# square qualification in
# fpga/kv260_v09_bram/evidence/board_2026-10-24_3a352d326c0a/). The class
# routes by size and route type:
# - n,m <= 128 on a FULL route: fpga/kv260_v09_bram unconditionally. The
#   event-heavy exception is deleted. Measured basis: ED fleet n=10 and
#   n=40 at m=2, FULL, 12.4 and 15.2 percent faster than v08 at the same
#   kernel_hz_measured 199999998, and square T=16..80 at 1.37-2.00x v08.
#   The event-heavy band between n=41 and n=128 is unmeasured; the
#   measured advantage grows with n (12.4 percent at n=10, 15.2 percent
#   at n=40) and the square points at n=m=16..80 bracket it at
#   1.37-2.00x, so the extrapolation runs in v09b's favour.
# - n or m above 128: fpga/kv260_v08 (FULL square cap 320, CG 372,
#   STREAM 1024). The BRAM image rejects an over-cap CONFIGURE with
#   ERR_BAD_DIMENSIONS.
# - a non-FULL route (CG or STREAM) at any size: fpga/kv260_v08, because
#   the BRAM image carries no such datapath and rejects it with
#   ERR_CAPACITY.
# - the legacy row-interleave image (board app snn_qp_solve, MAXN/MAXM 128)
#   implements the RETIRED pre-v0.5.0 box route (rows-only sweep, clip
#   after; a POCS failure the library fixed with facets-in-sweep) and is
#   reproduction-only for published numbers under matched-semantics
#   goldens, never a new paper's headline arm.
# Every measured polyhedral arm still records n, m, and events per outer
# iteration beside the package name. events/iter no longer selects the
# route. It is kept for audit.
# Quote the kernel clock as the clock record's kernel_hz_measured, never
# pl0_ref: on a clk_wiz app pl0_ref is the wizard INPUT (both kernels'
# board apps run pl0_ref 250 MHz through a 0.8 ratio to a true 200 MHz
# kernel clock).
polyhedral:
  package: fpga/kv260_v08
  boundary: fpga/kv260_v08/README.md
  cpu_baseline: fpga/cpu_baseline/cpu_baseline.cpp
  datapath_width_source: fpga/kv260_v08/src/dt.h
  qualified: 2026-10-11
  bram_package: fpga/kv260_v09_bram
  bram_boundary: fpga/kv260_v09_bram/README.md
  bram_datapath_width_source: fpga/kv260_v09_bram/src/dt.h
  bram_qualified: 2026-10-24
#
# cpu_baseline: none means no qualified same-solver CPU harness exists for
# that class; extend and requalify one (T-snn.10 point 2).
conic:
  package: fpga/kv260_v07
  boundary: fpga/kv260_v07/README.md
  cpu_baseline: none
  datapath_width_source: fpga/kv260_v07/src/dt.h
  qualified: 2026-09-24
